      "problem": "Find the roots of the parabola shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/87ed924d518696b8d9f442df341700aab36b8bedfbdee88269c94e54eb8a4478.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola. \n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-2,0)$ and $(4,0).$ \n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4.$",
